---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout title="How to Start an Activewear Brand" description="From zero to selling: the step-by-step roadmap for building a profitable activewear brand in 2024-2025. Learn product sourcing, branding, pricing, and marketing.">
  <section style="background:var(--color-primary);color:white;">
    <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;text-align:center;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size:1.5rem;">🚀</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-accent-light);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);padding:0.2rem 0.75rem;border-radius:9999px;">All Levels</span>
        <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#94a3b8;">12 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size:2.25rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:1rem;">How to Start an Activewear Brand</h1>
      <p style="color:#94a3b8;max-width:42rem;margin:0 auto;">From zero to selling: the step-by-step roadmap for building a profitable activewear brand in 2024-2025. Learn product sourcing, branding, pricing, and marketing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div style="max-width:56rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem;">
    <div style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:1rem;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Start With Research, Not Inventory</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Before buying any stock, spend 2-4 weeks studying the market. Use TikTok to identify trending styles (search #activewear, #yogapants). Check Amazon Best Seller Rank (BSR) for categories with consistent sales. Look at Shopify stores using BuiltWith to see what tools successful brands use. Your goal: find an underserved niche or a proven winner with room to differentiate.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Select Your Business Model</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Three viable paths: (1) Dropshipping - order 10-20 pieces per style, ship directly to customers. Low risk, lower margins. (2) Wholesale stocking - buy 50-200 pieces, hold inventory. Better margins, requires capital. (3) Brand building - custom designs with your logo. Highest margins, highest MOQ (300+). Start with option 1 or 2, migrate to option 3 once you have cash flow.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Source Your First Products</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">undefined</p>
      <ul style="margin-top:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;"><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Use a specialist supplier: Alibaba has general manufacturers; look for factories that specialize in activewear only</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Request samples from 3-5 suppliers before deciding</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Check their export history: do they ship to USA, UK, EU regularly?</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Verify factory certifications: OEKO-TEX, BSCI, ISO 9001</li><li style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Negotiate payment terms: 30% deposit, 70% before shipment for first orders</li></ul>
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Build Your Brand Identity</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">Your brand is more than a logo. Define: (1) Target customer (age, income, fitness level, values), (2) Brand personality (premium vs accessible, bold vs minimal), (3) Color palette and visual style. Use Canva or hire a freelancer on Fiverr for logo design ($50-200). Your product photos and social media content must feel consistent with this identity.</p>
      
      
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-top:2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Set Your Pricing Strategy</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.8;">For wholesale leggings at $8-12/unit: price at $35-55 for Amazon/e-commerce (3-4x cost), $45-65 for boutique/retail (4-5x cost). Your target customers are: budget-conscious fitness enthusiasts ($30-40), quality-focused buyers ($45-60), premium/luxury seekers ($65-100). Start at the middle to build trust, then raise prices once you have reviews.</p>
      
      
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:1.25rem;text-align:center;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How much money do I need to start an activewear brand?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">You can start with as little as $500-1,500 using dropshipping (order samples and forward to customers). For wholesale stocking, $2,000-5,000 covers initial inventory of 50-100 pieces per style. For custom branded products, budget $5,000-10,000 for MOQ production of 300+ pieces.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">Do I need a business license to sell activewear?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">In most countries, you can start as a sole proprietor without a business license. However, to sell on Amazon FBA you need a business entity and VAT registration in the EU. We strongly recommend setting up an LLC or limited company for liability protection once you exceed $1,000/month in revenue.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">Where should I sell my activewear products?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Start with one channel and master it: TikTok Shop for trending styles and viral growth, Amazon for search-based demand, Shopify for brand building and higher margins, Instagram for boutique and fitness influencer partnerships. Diversify once you have consistent sales in your first channel.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">How do I create a product photoshoot without a big budget?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">Use a smartphone on a tripod in natural light (near a window). Lay products on a white sheet or use a lightbox ($30 on Amazon). Take 20-30 photos per product from different angles. Use Snapseed or Canva to edit brightness and contrast. For lifestyle shots, ask friends to model or use flat-lay photography.</div>
      </details>
      
      <details style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:0.75rem;overflow:hidden;">
        <summary style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;gap:1rem;">
          <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);font-size:0.9rem;">What certifications do I need to sell activewear?</span>
          <svg style="width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;color:var(--color-text-light);flex-shrink:0;" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);">For US sales: CPSIA testing for children activewear, general product safety for adults. For EU sales: REACH compliance. For Amazon FBA: OEKO-TEX fabric safety certificates. Most specialist activewear factories already hold these certifications - ask for copies of their test reports before ordering.</div>
      </details>
      
    </div>

    <div style="background:var(--color-secondary);border-radius:1.5rem;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-primary);margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Have More Questions?</h2>
      <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--color-text-light);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Get personalized answers for your specific business on WhatsApp.</p>
      <a href={SITE.whatsappLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;background:var(--color-whatsapp);color:white;padding:0.875rem 2rem;border-radius:9999px;font-weight:700;">Ask on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much money do I need to start an activewear brand?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "You can start with as little as $500-1,500 using dropshipping (order samples and forward to customers). For wholesale stocking, $2,000-5,000 covers initial inventory of 50-100 pieces per style. For custom branded products, budget $5,000-10,000 for MOQ production of 300+ pieces."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do I need a business license to sell activewear?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In most countries, you can start as a sole proprietor without a business license. However, to sell on Amazon FBA you need a business entity and VAT registration in the EU. We strongly recommend setting up an LLC or limited company for liability protection once you exceed $1,000/month in revenue."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Where should I sell my activewear products?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Start with one channel and master it: TikTok Shop for trending styles and viral growth, Amazon for search-based demand, Shopify for brand building and higher margins, Instagram for boutique and fitness influencer partnerships. Diversify once you have consistent sales in your first channel."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I create a product photoshoot without a big budget?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Use a smartphone on a tripod in natural light (near a window). Lay products on a white sheet or use a lightbox ($30 on Amazon). Take 20-30 photos per product from different angles. Use Snapseed or Canva to edit brightness and contrast. For lifestyle shots, ask friends to model or use flat-lay photography."
        }
    },
    {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What certifications do I need to sell activewear?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For US sales: CPSIA testing for children activewear, general product safety for adults. For EU sales: REACH compliance. For Amazon FBA: OEKO-TEX fabric safety certificates. Most specialist activewear factories already hold these certifications - ask for copies of their test reports before ordering."
        }
    }
],
  })} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": SITE.url },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Resources", "item": SITE.url + "/resources" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "How to Start an Activewear Brand", "item": SITE.url + "/resources/how-to-start-activewear-brand" },
    ],
  })} />
</BaseLayout>
